{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\n\n#define dbg(x) cerr << #x << \" = \" << (x) << endl\n#define raya cerr << \"-------------------\" << endl\n\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef long long ll;\n\nstruct step {\n\tll val; int cost;\n\tbool operator<(const step &c) const {\n\t\treturn c.cost < cost;\n\t}\n};\n\nset<ll> visited;\n\nbool wasVisited(ll c) {\n\treturn visited.find(c) != visited.end();\n}\n\nstep uupper(ll n){\n\tll res = 0;\n\tint i = 0;\n\twhile(res<n){\n\t\tres*=10;\n\t\tres++;\n\t\ti++;\n\t}\n\treturn {res, i};\n}\n\nstep upper(ll n){\n\tll res = 0;\n\tint i = 0;\n\twhile(res*10+1<=n){\n\t\tres*=10;\n\t\tres++;\n\t\ti++;\n\t}\n\tll resmul = res;\n\tint imul = i;\n\twhile(res < n){\n\t\tres+=resmul;\n\t\ti+=imul;\n\t}\n\treturn {res, i};\n}\n\nstep lower(ll n){\n\tll res = 0;\n\tint i = 0;\n\twhile(res*10+1<=n){\n\t\tres*=10;\n\t\tres++;\n\t\ti++;\n\t}\n\tll resmul = res;\n\tint imul = i;\n\twhile(res+resmul <= n){\n\t\tres+=resmul;\n\t\ti+=imul;\n\t}\n\treturn {res, i};\n}\n\nint main(int argc, char **argv) {\n\tll n;\n\tcin >> n;\n\n\tpriority_queue<step> pq;\n\n\tpq.push(step{n, 0});\n\n\twhile(pq.top().val != 0){\n\t\tll val = pq.top().val;\n\t\tint cost = pq.top().cost;\n\t\tpq.pop();\n\n\t\tif(wasVisited(val))\n\t\t\tcontinue;\n\t\tvisited.insert(val);\n\n\t\tfor (step next : { lower(val), upper(val), uupper(val) }) {\n\t\t\tnext.cost += cost;\n\t\t\tnext.val = abs(val - next.val);\n\t\t\tpq.push(next);\n\n\t\t}\n\n\t}\n\n\tcout << pq.top().cost << endl;\n}\n\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport heapq\n\ndef wasVisited(c, visited):\n    return c in visited\n\ndef uupper(n):\n    res = 0\n    i = 0\n    while res < n:\n        res = res * 10 + 1\n        i += 1\n    return (res, i)\n\ndef upper(n):\n    res = 0\n    i = 0\n    while res * 10 + 1 <= n:\n        res = res * 10 + 1\n        i += 1\n    resmul = res\n    imul = i\n    while res < n:\n        res += resmul\n        i += imul\n    return (res, i)\n\ndef lower(n):\n    res = 0\n    i = 0\n    while res * 10 + 1 <= n:\n        res = res * 10 + 1\n        i += 1\n    resmul = res\n    imul = i\n    while res + resmul <= n:\n        res += resmul\n        i += imul\n    return (res, i)\n\ndef main():\n    n = int(input().strip())\n    \n    visited = set()\n    # Priority queue: (cost, value)\n    pq = []\n    heapq.heappush(pq, (0, n))\n    \n    while pq:\n        cost, val = heapq.heappop(pq)\n        \n        if val == 0:\n            print(cost)\n            return\n        \n        if wasVisited(val, visited):\n            continue\n        visited.add(val)\n        \n        for next_val, next_cost in [lower(val), upper(val), uupper(val)]:\n            new_cost = cost + next_cost\n            new_val = abs(val - next_val)\n            heapq.heappush(pq, (new_cost, new_val))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00012575789878610522, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -2.38